Yiwu Market is known as the China Commodity City and is the largest wholesale market in the world, which can provide any buyer with suitable quantities and varieties at low price. Among them, Yiwu International Trade City (Futian Market) is the main market, operating 26 main categories and 2.1 million commodities, including toys, electronic products, household goods, jewelry, sports goods and other daily products.
Yiwu International Trade City was established in 1982 and consists of 5 major markets. Now it has a business area of over 6.4 million square meters, 75,000 stores, more than 210,000 employees, 210,000 passengers per day, 26 categories and 2.1 million individual products, and the products are sold to more than 200 countries and regions.
The construction area of the district 3 of the International Trade City is 460,000 square meters. The main market has more than 6,000 booths of 14 square meters on the 1-3 floors, more than 650 showrooms of 50 square meters or more on the 4-5 floors, and more than 8,000 commercial houses.
